# *** THIS FIXTURE IS DERIVED, NOT OBSERVED. ***
#
# EXPECTED VERDICT: FAIL.
# A report with 1,001 net discrepancies, so its discrepancy numbers run past
# 999 into four digits. DISC 1001 is the 23-August rzG defect - cache data bit
# 123 - copied verbatim from
# ci/fixtures/lvs-missing-connection/fail-observed-rzg-entry62. The 1,000
# entries before it are the compact `Net <n> / ** no similar net **` form
# Calibre prints for an unmatched layout net, copied in shape from
# ASIC/eth-chiplet/build/rc1eco-20260826/lvs_run (DISC 103-105 there); their
# net numbers are the invention.
#
# WHAT IT PROVES. Calibre's DISC# field is SEVEN CHARACTERS WIDE with the
# number right-justified in the first three, so the gap before the name column
# SHRINKS as the number grows: `  1    `, ` 10    `, `100    `, `1000   `,
# `18601  `. The parser used to hardcode ` {4}` after the number and therefore
# matched ONLY 1-to-3-digit numbers. On this fixture the unfixed parser reads
# DISC 1 to 999, never sees DISC 1000 or 1001, attributes DISC 1001's
# missing-connection row to DISC 999 - a top-level filler - and reports PASS
# on a report that contains the defect this gate was written for.
#
# AND THE CONTROL COULD NOT CATCH IT. N7 declares the discrepancy list
# saturated when the parsed count reaches `LVS REPORT MAXIMUM`, but the parser
# itself clipped that count at 999, so on a capped run N7 compared 999 against
# 1000 and passed. A gate proving its own coverage with a number it had
# already truncated. Mutation M14 restores ` {4}`; this arm catches it.
#
# Five-digit DISC numbers in INCORRECT NETS are not hypothetical on this site:
# ASIC/eth-chiplet/build/rc2-20260827 numbers that section 1 to 18,600.
#



